From: h0cheung <hcheunh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: drain scan completion before interface teardown

Scan completion is deferred to vdev_clean_wk. cancel_hw_scan waits for
firmware completion, but previously returned with that work still queued.
A following stop could cancel it without notifying mac80211, leaving
SCAN_HW_SCANNING set across suspend and all later scans returning EBUSY.
The observed failure has a cfg80211 NETDEV_DOWN warning followed by
"resume with hardware scan still in progress".

Drain the cleanup work with the wiphy lock held, as the driver's existing
cancel_remain_on_channel callback already does. If a range batch has
finished but cleanup is pending, mark the logical request aborting so
flushing the worker cannot start another batch during cancellation.
Keep the timeout-vs-normal-completion guard unchanged.

Link: https://github.com/mydanyi/armadaos-freedom/blob/244b74516d99d06cb0518609ce4b842ab278be8a/packages/kernel/patches/0188-wifi-ath12k-baldur-range-scans.patch
Link: https://github.com/mydanyi/armadaos-freedom/blob/244b74516d99d06cb0518609ce4b842ab278be8a/packages/kernel/patches/1021-wifi-ath12k-convert-scan-timeout-to-wiphy-delayed-work.patch
Signed-off-by: h0cheung <hcheunh@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
@@ -6228,7 +6228,18 @@
 
 		ath12k_scan_abort(ar);
 
+		/* A completed range batch may still have queued cleanup. Do not
+		 * start another batch while cancelling the logical scan.
+		 */
+		spin_lock_bh(&ar->data_lock);
+		if (ar->scan.range_req && ar->scan.finish_queued &&
+		    ar->scan.state == ATH12K_SCAN_RUNNING)
+			ar->scan.state = ATH12K_SCAN_ABORTING;
+		spin_unlock_bh(&ar->data_lock);
+
 		wiphy_delayed_work_cancel(hw->wiphy, &ar->scan.timeout);
+		/* Report completion before interface stop can cancel this work. */
+		wiphy_work_flush(hw->wiphy, &ar->scan.vdev_clean_wk);
 	}
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL(ath12k_mac_op_cancel_hw_scan);
